  "article": {
    "id": "re-foundations-3a-digging-for-the-past",
    "title": "RE Foundations / 3A / Digging for the Past",
    "text_type": "narrative",
    "audience": {
      "grade_band": "upper_elementary"
    },
    "language": "en"
  },
  "content": {
    "paragraphs": [
      {
        "id": "p1",
        "order": 1,
        "sentences": [
          {
            "id": "s1",
            "text": "When I was in third grade, I watched a video that recreated the discovery of King Tutankhamen’s tomb."
          },
          {
            "id": "s2",
            "text": "I remember Howard Carter 1 peering through a narrow hole in the tomb with a candle."
          },
          {
            "id": "s3",
            "text": "A workman asked what he could see: “Wonderful things!” Carter said."
          },
          {
            "id": "s4",
            "text": "From that moment, I knew what I wanted to do with my life."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p2",
        "order": 2,
        "sentences": [
          {
            "id": "s5",
            "text": "Today, I’m lucky to work as an archeologist."
          },
          {
            "id": "s6",
            "text": "I study the lives of people who lived in Egypt’s Nile Delta."
          },
          {
            "id": "s7",
            "text": "It’s exciting work."
          },
          {
            "id": "s8",
            "text": "Sometimes you find something that was buried three thousand years ago."
          },
          {
            "id": "s9",
            "text": "Holding a piece of history is an amazing feeling."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p3",
        "order": 3,
        "sentences": [
          {
            "id": "s10",
            "text": "So I decided what I wanted to be at the age of nine, and I made it happen."
          },
          {
            "id": "s11",
            "text": "Seems easy, right?"
          },
          {
            "id": "s12",
            "text": "Not quite!"
          },
          {
            "id": "s13",
            "text": "The road wasn’t easy."
          },
          {
            "id": "s14",
            "text": "I did my studies—university, then a PhD."
          },
          {
            "id": "s15",
            "text": "But along the way I was told many things: I was too young, I wasn’t qualified, I should get married and have kids."
          },
          {
            "id": "s16",
            "text": "I also needed money, so I applied for six grants."
          },
          {
            "id": "s18",
            "text": "Six months later, the last reply came: This time it was yes."
          },
          {
            "id": "s19",
            "text": "Finally, I could start my own excavation."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p4",
        "order": 4,
        "sentences": [
          {
            "id": "s20",
            "text": "For anyone thinking about a career, I would say: Never give up."
          },
          {
            "id": "s21",
            "text": "If you want to do something, keep trying."
          },
          {
            "id": "s22",
            "text": "If people tell you no, use that—it will push you."
          },
          {
            "id": "s23",
            "text": "At the beginning, it hurts."
          },
          {
            "id": "s24",
            "text": "But the next no hurts a little less."
          },
          {
            "id": "s25",
            "text": "It makes you stronger and actually helps you."
          },
          {
            "id": "s26",
            "text": "Second, focus on your goals."
          },
          {
            "id": "s27",
            "text": "And I stress yours."
          },
          {
            "id": "s28",
            "text": "You don’t have to follow other people."
          },
          {
            "id": "s29",
            "text": "If they say something has never been done, make it happen."
          },
          {
            "id": "s30",
            "text": "You may be the first to do it!"
          },
          {
            "id": "s31",
            "text": "There are always challenges, but you overcome them in the end."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p5",
        "order": 5,
        "sentences": [
          {
            "id": "s32",
            "text": "1 Howard Carter was a British archeologist who became famous for discovering the tomb of Tutankhamen in 1922."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
